SWEET Bluetooth: boot-arg sweetbtnopcf=1 (patch 0231, ticket T-b58f, W-BTSCAN), diagnostic knob, default off, no change without it: bluetoothd's HCI vendor command 0xfce9 with sub-op 05 (_BCM_LEMetaPCFServiceUUID) or 07 (_BCM_LEMetaScanFilterUUID) is not sent to the chip and bluetoothd gets the Command Complete the chip gave for the same sub-op + action in bt-up14, injected by the rx thread only between chip events (the 0217 H4 framer, now also on with this knob). bt-up14 [obs 20261107T121323Z-bt-up14]: with the filter installed the chip reported 0 LE advertisements in 256 s, the same 200b/200c bytes without it 13 in 20 s. The tx parser (0226) now copies into an out buffer so a command can be held until its sub-op + action byte are known; unknown action, a lost rx framer or a full answer queue send the command unchanged with a BT GAP row. Review T-b58f-0231 F1: the rx side (framer + answer delivery) runs on its own flag sbu_nopcf_rx that the tx parser never clears, so answers queued before a tx-parser stop still drain; F3: a lost framer names sweetbtnopcf; the boot-arg parse is its own function (host-tested). Fewer bytes reach the chip; no register store added.

